cat <<'EOF'
Installing Bingux OS
====================

1. Connect to the network. Ethernet and known Wi-Fi networks connect on their
   own; for Wi-Fi run nmtui.
2. Find the disk to install onto:
       bingux-installer probe
   This prints the disks as JSON.
3. Write a plan file, plan.json, with the disk, the user accounts, hostname,
   timezone, locale and keymap. See `bingux-installer --help` for the format.
4. Install. This ERASES the disk, so check the name twice:
       sudo bingux-installer install --plan plan.json
5. Reboot, remove the USB stick, and sign in at the Bingux login screen.

Project and documentation: https://github.com/kierandrewett/bingux
EOF
